acceptance_criteria: Package installs with pm install; npm release gate passes; changelog is generated from package-local pm data; tracked files and reachable git history have no secret pattern hits.
risk: medium
confidence: high
release: 0.1.0
resolution: Completed the original 2026-05-26 release-hardening scope; later full-history privacy evidence is tracked as an independent future-publication blocker.
expected_result: Package-local release tooling and checks are established while later evidence can supersede publication approval without erasing historical changelog records.
actual_result: The original hardening remains implemented and its historical changelog entry is retained; the 2026-08-20 all-ref audit independently blocks future publication through pm-csv-uaq1.
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T19:38:43.301Z",codex,"Superseding evidence: the 2026-08-20 all-ref audit invalidates the earlier release-readiness statement for reachable history. Current tree checks remain clean; publication is blocked by pm-csv-uaq1 until the maintainer authorizes and coordinates history repair."
  "2026-08-20T19:53:27.138Z",codex,PR 73 CodeRabbit correctly noted that the retained body contradicted the newer all-ref finding and that reopening a released item erased its historical changelog entry. The body is now truthful; this historical task is re-closed while pm-csv-uaq1 remains the active future-publication blocker.
  "2026-08-20T19:56:10.790Z",codex,Corrected completed_at back to the original 2026-05-26 completion boundary so pm-changelog preserves the historical release entry instead of reclassifying it as new Unreleased work.
